  "notes": "Cash basis city. The statements show the Sewer fund among the governmental funds (one column per fund); per the rule for cash-basis fund-column statements the Sewer column is recorded as business-type: its receipts (charges for services 663,866; sewer part 239,908 of Licenses, fees, and permits), its disbursements (Public works - sewer 542,322) and its balances (964,314 -> 1,325,766, p4) are in business_type, and governmental totals/balances are the Total Governmental column (p5) minus the Sewer column (p4). Fund balances statement p3 lacks the Debt Service/Total column page in the trim, so the balance sheet uses the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1); cash in bank split into governmental and Sewer (Sewer cash 1,325,766 from p3). The error correction (Note 13) moves 15,554 from General to TIF beginning balances and nets to zero in total, so no adjustment is recorded. No transfers. Detail: General Fund by department combining schedule (p7-8). The all-funds budget schedule (p6) is not recorded: it is not by fund and would double count the General Fund; other funds have no own schedule (user 2026-10-28: no statement lines added). Read pages 1-8 of 8."
